  identity: "completion_predicate_satisfied_by_the_empty_population" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**A completion or coverage predicate whose EMPTINESS IS INDISTINGUISHABLE FROM ITS SATISFACTION.** `nothing outstanding` over a population of nothing answers the same as `nothing outstanding` over a population that was examined, and the failure is always toward DONE. The moment the population is empty is typically the moment work was just started or a head just pushed, which is precisely when someone is waiting on the answer. ",

    "**THE REPO ALREADY REFUSES THIS CLASS AT ONE SITE, IN WRITING, AND DOES NOT APPLY IT AT THE ADJACENT ONE. THE NEIGHBOURING PAIR IS THE ARGUMENT.** ",

    "SITE WITH THE GUARD -- `required_floor_runner`'s expected-red roster decode refuses `ExpectedRedRosterEmpty` when the roster evaluates to zero identities, and states why: `an empty roster makes the partition-sum and did-not-execute checks vacuous, so every enrolled row reports as an ordinary failure and no guard can fire`. Its surrounding comment names the shape exactly -- `a read failure quietly wearing the same face as success`. ",

    "SITE WITHOUT IT, AND IT IS THE MERGE-BLOCKING ONE -- `claim_executor` `required_floor_outcome_is_clean` is a conjunction of ELEVEN `.is_empty()` terms with no denominator anywhere in it. Zero planned claims satisfies all eleven and returns clean. ",

    "**THE PROTECTION CITED IN THE CODE IS TRUE AND VACUOUS IN EXACTLY THE CASE IT NAMES.** `run_required_floor` is documented as refusing `when planned, executed and terminal identity counts disagree, so a silently short roster cannot report as a pass`. At zero that invariant reads `0 == 0 + 0`. It holds, it is advertised as what covers a short roster, and it is satisfied by the roster being absent entirely. ",

    "**STRUCTURAL VACUITY IS ESTABLISHED; REACHABILITY IS NOT, AND THE ROW CLAIMS ONLY THE FIRST.** Whether any route can drive the floor to a zero planned population is untraced -- a `FloorDiscoveryRefused` arm may close every one of them. What is established is that the completion predicate is satisfied by the empty population and that the invariant named as covering that case does not cover it. ",

    "THREE EXTERNAL RECEIPTS, ALL IN LANE TOOLING RATHER THAN REPO CODE, ALL FAILING TOWARD DONE, ALL ON ONE EVENING: a `case` partition over a check conclusion where running checks rendered EMPTY and the catch-all arm was TERMINAL, reporting SETTLED with five checks in progress; a monitor printing `pending=0 failing=[]` for a pull request whose rollup was empty, written an HOUR AFTER that first instance was written up, using the corrected predicate; and a watch whose condition was `no pending checks`, satisfied by no checks at all on a just-force-pushed head, reporting CONCLUDED forty minutes early. ",

    "**TWO OF THE THREE WERE WRITTEN AFTER THE CLASS HAD BEEN WRITTEN DOWN, WHICH IS WHAT DECIDES THE REMEDY.** Knowing the class did not protect the next instrument either author wrote, so it does not belong in anyone's attention -- it belongs in the predicate. ",

    "**NEXT TRIGGER, NAMED AS THE CAPABILITY AND WITH WHAT IT MUST BE SUFFICIENT FOR:** every completion or coverage predicate on the required floor requires a POSITIVE DENOMINATOR, so a zero-size population refuses as NOT-YET-STARTED rather than passing as settled -- sufficient for no `FloorClean` verdict being derivable from an empty planned population. Adding one guard at `claims_planned` is the artifact-grained version and discharges nothing: it leaves the class alive at every predicate nobody has enumerated. ",

